          %h2#equivariant_version Equivariant version
          %p
            In
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+homotopy+theory"} equivariant homotopy theory
            the statement is that
            = succeed "-homotopy" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-CW+complexes"} G-CW complexes
            are equivalent to maps that are weak homotopy equivalences on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fixed+point"} fixed point
            spaces
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^H
            for all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+subset"} closed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subgroups"} subgroups
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H \subset G
            (e.g.
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#GreenleesMay95"} Greenlees-May 95, theorem 2.4
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+Whitehead+theorem"} equivariant Whitehead theorem
          %h2#in_general_toposes
            In general
            = succeed "-toposes" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          %p
            There is a notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+groups"} homotopy groups
            for objects in every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-stack"} ∞-stack
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+group+%28of+an+%E2%88%9E-stack%29"} homotopy group (of an ∞-stack)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+homotopy+equivalence"} weak homotopy equivalence
            in every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-stack"} ∞-stack
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            and hence an analog of the statement of Whiteheads theorem. One finds that
          %p
            %strong Warning
            Whitehead’s theorem
            %strong fails
            for general
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-toposes"} (∞,1)-toposes
            and non-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/truncated+object+in+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} truncated
            objects.
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-stack"} ∞-stack
            = succeed "es" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            = succeed "es." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hypercomplete+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} hypercomplete (∞,1)-topos
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} presented
            by a local
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} model structure on simplicial presheaves
          %p
            For instance the hypercomplete
            = succeed "-topos" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
            is presented by the model structure on simplicial presheaves on the point, namely the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} model structure on simplicial sets
          %h2#in_homotopy_type_theory In homotopy type theory
          %p
            Since
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
            admits models in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-toposes"} (∞,1)-toposes
            (and in particular in non-hypercomplete ones), Whitehead’s theorem is not provable when regarded as a statement about types in homotopy type theory. From this perspective, the truth of Whitehead’s theorem is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/foundational+axiom"} foundational axiom
            that may be regarded as a “classicality” property, akin to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/excluded+middle"} excluded middle
            or the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
            — we call it
            %strong Whitehead’s principle
            (not to be confused with
            = succeed "," do
              %span.newWikiWord
                Whitehead's problem
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Whitehead%27s+problem"} ?
          %p
            Whitehead’s principle does hold, however, for maps between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+n-types"} homotopy n-types
            for any finite
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/induction"} induction
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mod+p+Whitehead+theorem"} mod p Whitehead theorem
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+Whitehead+theorem"} equivariant Whitehead theorem
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "G-spectrum#EquivariantWhitehead"} equivariant stable Whitehead theorem
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW-approximation+theorem"} CW-approximation theorem
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cellular+approximation+theorem"} cellular approximation theorem
          %h2#references References
          %p
            The original theorem for maps between
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW+complexes"} CW complexes
          %ul
            %li#Whitehead49
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J.+H.+C.+Whitehead"}> J. H. C. Whitehead
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Combinatorial homotopy. I
              %strong 55
              3 (1949) 213–245 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.1090/s0002-9904-1949-09175-9"}> doi:10.1090/s0002-9904-1949-09175-9
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.ams.org/journals/bull/1949-55-03/S0002-9904-1949-09175-9/S0002-9904-1949-09175-9.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            The version in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+homotopy+theory"} simplicial homotopy theory
            is due to:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+M.+Kan"}> Daniel M. Kan
              , Theorem 7.2 in:
              = succeed "," do
                %em On c.s.s. categories
              %strong 2
              (1957) 82–94 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://www.boletin.math.org.mx/pdf/2/2/BSMM(2).2.82-94.pdf"}> pdf
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://dmitripavlov.org/scans/kan-on-css-categories.pdf"} pdf
          %p Review:
          %ul
            %li#Bredon93
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Glen+Bredon"}> Glen Bredon
                , Cor. 11.14 in:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Topology and Geometry
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 139
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-1-4757-6848-0"} doi:10.1007/978-1-4757-6848-0
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://virtualmath1.stanford.edu/~ralph/math215b/Bredon.pdf"} pdf
            %li#ElmendorfKrizMay95
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Anthony+Elmendorf"}> Anthony Elmendorf
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Igor+Kriz"} Igor Kriz
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+May"} Peter May
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Modern+foundations+for+stable+homotopy+theory"} Modern foundations for stable homotopy theory
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ioan+Mackenzie+James"} Ioan Mackenzie James
                (ed.),
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Handbook+of+Algebraic+Topology"} Handbook of Algebraic Topology
                (1995) 213-253 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://hopf.math.purdue.edu/Elmendorf-Kriz-May/modern_foundations.pdf"}> pdf
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li#Hatcher02
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Allen+Hatcher"}> Allen Hatcher
                , pp. 346 in:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Algebraic Topology
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.cambridge.org/gb/academic/subjects/mathematics/geometry-and-topology/algebraic-topology-1?format=PB=9780521795401"} ISBN:9780521795401
                = succeed "]" do
                  %a{:href => "https://pi.math.cornell.edu/~hatcher/AT/ATpage.html"} webpage
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marcelo+Aguilar"}> Marcelo Aguilar
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Samuel+Gitler"} Samuel Gitler
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Carlos+Prieto"} Carlos Prieto
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Algebraic topology from a homotopical viewpoint
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/b97586"} doi:10.1007/b97586
          %p
            Discussion of the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+Whitehead+theorem"} equivariant Whitehead theorem
          %ul
            %li#GreenleesMay95
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Greenlees"}> John Greenlees
              ,
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+May"} Peter May
              = succeed "," do
                %em Equivariant stable homotopy theory
              %em Handbook of Algebraic Topology
              (1995) 279-325 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://www.math.uchicago.edu/~may/PAPERS/Newthird.pdf"}> pdf
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-topos"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              \-topos
            theoretic version:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
              , section 6.5 of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} Higher Topos Theory
          %p
            The analogous formulation in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
          %ul
            %li#UFP13
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Univalent+Foundations+Project"}> Univalent Foundations Project
              , §8.8 in:
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Homotopy+Type+Theory+--+Univalent+Foundations+of+Mathematics"} Homotopy Type Theory – Univalent Foundations of Mathematics
              (2013) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://homotopytypetheory.org/book/"}> web
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://hottheory.files.wordpress.com/2013/03/hott-online-323-g28e4374.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            Corresponding formalization in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Agda"} Agda
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dan+Licata"}> Dan Licata
              ,
              %em
                %a{:href => "https://github.com/dlicata335/hott-agda/blob/master/homotopy/Whitehead.agda"} Whitehead.agda
          .property
            category:
            %a.category_link{:href => "/nlab/all_pages/foundational+axiom"} foundational axiom
